<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shuqra</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Shoqra</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shuqra is a small port town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-aden">Gulf of Aden</a> in the Abyan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a> of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a>. From the late 17th century it was the chief town of the Fadhli Sultanate, whose sultans controlled the coast and hinterland of Abyan. Under British protection from the 19th century, the sultanate joined the Federation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-arabia">South Arabia</a> before being absorbed into independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-yemen">South Yemen</a> in 1967.</p></div>
